[[1,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>Position the vehicle on the ramp.</p><p>1. Remove the cap (1a), undo the bolt (1b) and remove the single\nbelt fixed tensioner (1c).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001806.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[1,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Place the engine components single drive\nbelt fixed tensioner back in its housing and fix it tightening the bolt\nto the recommended torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>FIXED SINGLE SERVICE BELT TENSIONER</p></td><td><p>M10</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>4.5 ÷ 5.5</p></td></tr></table></div><p>Place the plug back in its housing in the\nfixed tensioner.</p><p>Remove the car from the ramp.</p>"],[2,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>Position the vehicle on the ramp.</p><p>1. Undo the bolts (1a) and remove the crankshaft pulley (1b).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2002175.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2,63,0,"<p>1. Remove the cap (1a), undo the bolt (1b) and remove the single\nbelt fixed tensioner (1c).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2002176.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[2,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Place the engine components single drive\nbelt fixed tensioner back in its housing and fix it tightening the bolt\nto the recommended torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>FIXED SINGLE SERVICE BELT TENSIONER</p></td><td><p>M10</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>4.5 ÷ 5.5</p></td></tr></table></div><p>Place the plug back in its housing in the\nfixed tensioner.</p><p>Place the crankshaft pulley back in its\nhousing and secure it tightening the bolts to the recommended torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>CRANKSHAFT PULLEY</p></td><td><p>M8</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>2.3 ÷ 2.8</p></td></tr></table></div><p>Remove the car from the ramp.</p>"],[8,63,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"re